Of course. It's getting colder.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.520
It's hibernation time.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.580
And it's even colder up here, Chris.

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:16.720
We've got the first snowstorm of the season.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.270
This must be why they left in the first place.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.610
Right, guys? Guys?

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.540
They couldn't survive up there.

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:26.820
But here, they can huddle together through the winter.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.400
And so are we.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:29.960
Butterf...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:30.760
Butterfly style.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.160
Migrators turned hibernators.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:41.580
Well, if they hang out with the sleeping butterflies for four months,

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:45.320
it'll give me time to work on butterfly programming for the creature power suits.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:46.890
Sweet dreams.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:50.880
This isn't Mexico.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.560
This isn't Mexico.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:10.940
Mexico!

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:20.050
Finally, Mexico.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.110
It took me four months, but it was worth the wait.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:24.630
Now hurry up!

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:43.240
Back off! Wait, who are you talking to?

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.740
Whoa, sorry. I just had a nightmare.

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.350
I dreamt Danita was here taking branchfuls of butterflies.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:52.190
Chris, I don't think that was a dream! Look!

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:52.810
Oh no!

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.260
Oh, you're just trying to get a good four months sleep

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.340
and Danita snatches you just so you're about to wake up and head home.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.040
It's true, look. Everyone's waking up.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.930
Oh, morning, Maxzilla. Glad you're here.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.480
Come in, Tortuga HQ.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.250
Oh, hello, sleeping beauties. Welcome to spring.

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:12.930
Aviva, where's Danita?

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:16.900
I don't know. I've been so busy adding butterfly programming to the suits.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.660
Last report, she was wandering around the Arctic.

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.520
She'll never find that secret forest.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:25.060
Well, this is never, and the secret's out.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.300
Oh, no. You guys use your suits. They're done.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:29.980
We're away. We'll...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:33.080
Hey, Teleport!

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.880
I got it!

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.020
Debate!

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.210
Not Caterpillar Mode!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:46.730
Ah!

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:49.500
That's Betterfly!

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:50.840
I mean Butterfly!

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:51.600
Chris?

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:52.590
Oh, no.

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.120
Crystal is Mode!

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.190
My Power!

00:18:59.210 --> 00:18:59.970
The Creature Red!

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:05.710
I'm tired of delays.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.290
I need to get these butterflies back to the mansion.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.740
Aw, Gracie.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:16.030
Hey, looking good.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.260
Dabio!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.780
Yes, beautiful barrettes.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:26.900
Soon everyone will be wearing them.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:27.460
What?

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.860
What is happening to my butterfly?

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:35.870
No d-ing! I order you to stop d-

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.810
Maxilla! Wake up! Are you okay?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.630
Wake up! I'll do a medical check!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.930
No! I think she's- she's dying!

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:57.670
No Maxilla! Don't! You can't do that!

00:19:58.440 --> 00:19:59.980
Martin over here! She-

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:06.500
laid an egg and look so she a new generation of monarchs is on the way in

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:11.210
just four days these monarch eggs will hatch into tiny caterpillars and start

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:18.740
the whole life cycle over again lay eggs and then die I know it's just how life is

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:25.270
for lots of insects yeah but she lived a super long life bro four months 3,000

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:29.880
miles maxilla saw more of the world than most people do yeah

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.980
All that, and she never made it back home.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.380
What if she's not supposed to make it home?

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:40.580
Yeah, maybe he's supposed to keep the journey going.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.200
Yes, nature's got know-how.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:47.090
They lay eggs so the babies can continue the journey home.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.560
Martin, Chris, I found Donita.

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:53.550
I think she's killing all the butterflies.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:54.890
It's not Donita.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.270
The butterflies are just doing their natural butterfly thing.

00:20:58.470 --> 00:20:59.530
It's their life cycle.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:04.670
But we've got to rescue them so they can lay eggs and keep that life cycle going.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.060
And I've got a plan that might work.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:12.150
Do not die on me now. I need living butterfly barrettes.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.970
Do you hear me? Living!

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.710
At least they're easier to catch now.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.360
Not as easy as you are.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.660
Doing me out of here!

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:26.980
You kept trying to net these monarchs. Now it's your turn.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.640
But I still have the butterflies.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:31.430
How are you going to get them?

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:32.740
Like this?

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:33.950
Milkweed anyone?

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:37.830
Beautiful butterfly!

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:39.520
Follow us!

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:41.740
We'd know of a great milkweed patch.

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:45.200
No, no, no, I can't with my butterflies.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.960
I had idea we're butterfly barrettes anyway.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:08.870
Don't answer that.

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:12.890
Ah, the thing every monarch needs to lay its eggs.

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:14.230
A milkweed patch.

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:20.990
And when they hatch, those milkweed-eating caterpillars of yours will have a feast!

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.540
Wow, the life cycle of the migrating monarch is saved.

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.790
So let me get this straight, guys.

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:29.980
The butterflies that lived during the fall...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.080
migrate 3,000 miles to Mexico to escape the cold.

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:37.220
And when they get to their secret forest, they hibernate.

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:38.680
Then they wake up in the spring,

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:41.020
just as the milkweed is starting to grow back.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:43.400
But they don't make it all the way home.

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:46.240
It's their sons and daughters who will finish the trip.

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:50.130
They lay eggs before they die that will hatch into caterpillars.

00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:53.650
The caterpillar eats and eats, forms a chrysalis,

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:56.120
and finally becomes a butterfly.

00:22:56.880 --> 00:22:59.620
The sons and daughters of those original butterflies

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.540
will continue the journey home.

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:05.190
That is one incredible life story.

00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:10.770
The new generation of monarchs is here.

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:13.320
Safe and sound and heading north.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:15.230
Look at them go!

00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:18.180
Hi, Maxzilla Jr.

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:19.460
You're doing great.

00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:21.510
Ah, your mom would be proud.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:23.930
With their own creature know-how,

00:23:24.110 --> 00:23:25.750
and a little help from friends like us,

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:28.390
little creatures can do amazing things.

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:29.810
Woo!

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:38.630
So monarch butterflies have what it takes to make one of the greatest migrations in

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:39.490
the creature world.

00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:43.070
Right now is the beginning of fall, and the monarch migration is underway.

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:47.070
And we're here at an important pit stop place for migrating monarchs.

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:48.410
Why is it so important?

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:50.770
That's why.

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:54.960
This huge body of water is what the monarch butterflies have to cross.

00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:58.640
Lake Erie, 100 miles across.

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:04.140
That group of monarchs has spent the night roosting in the trees.

00:24:04.320 --> 00:24:07.080
They're resting up for their journey across the lake.

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.560
And as the sun warms up their bodies,

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:12.360
they begin to move and work their muscles.

00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:16.560
One by one, they take off.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:23.060
Butterflies also fuel up here.

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:25.120
They drink nectar from the flowers

00:24:25.120 --> 00:24:28.500
to get the energy they need to make it across the lake.

00:24:29.220 --> 00:24:29.980
Get a good drink.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.980
Oh, there he goes!

00:24:33.560 --> 00:24:34.040
Alright!

00:24:36.010 --> 00:24:37.870
Before they cross, they'll check the wind.

00:24:38.070 --> 00:24:41.150
If it's blowing south, it'll help them across the lake.

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:43.030
There he goes!

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:43.670
He's ready!

00:24:44.310 --> 00:24:44.830
Good luck!

00:24:46.540 --> 00:24:48.720
With the forests in Mexico being cut down,

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.740
and more and more habitat along the way being destroyed,

00:24:52.100 --> 00:24:54.420
the monarchs could use a lot of help from us.

00:24:55.720 --> 00:24:58.320
One thing you can do is plant a butterfly garden.

00:24:58.500 --> 00:24:59.980
Your own pit stop place...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.380
for migrating monarchs.

00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:06.700
Monarchs love to fuel up on butterfly bush and the sea.

00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:10.560
You can also help monarchs by helping scientists

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:11.980
track their migration.

00:25:12.220 --> 00:25:13.300
Tag a monarch.

00:25:13.690 --> 00:25:15.690
That way, scientists can track

00:25:15.690 --> 00:25:17.890
an individual monarch's journey.

00:25:18.090 --> 00:25:22.530
This monarch's ID is NEC650.

00:25:22.910 --> 00:25:25.550
Then when you tag the monarch, hold it gently

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:27.530
by the leading edge of its wings

00:25:27.530 --> 00:25:29.690
and put the little tiny tag

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:36.680
right on this part of the lower wing there the tags light and won't bother the monarch when she's

00:25:36.680 --> 00:25:43.230
flying and if this monarch makes it all the way down to mexico a scientist may find her and because

00:25:43.230 --> 00:25:51.900
of the tag know exactly where she was released and when you ready to fly there he goes have a

00:25:51.900 --> 00:25:59.500
good trip bon voyage monarch butterflies little creatures that can do big things we'll see on the

